= Principal–agent problem — Technical =

A stylized hidden-action model has principal payoff V(y)-w(y) and agent utility u(w(y))-c(e), where output y depends probabilistically on effort e that the principal cannot directly observe. Contract design trades off incentive provision, information, participation, and often risk sharing.

== Modeling cautions ==
* principal–agent problem ≠ employer–employee relationship only
* moral hazard ≠ adverse selection
* delegation ≠ guaranteed incentive alignment

== References ==
* Bengt Holmström, “Moral Hazard and Observability” (1979).
* Royal Swedish Academy of Sciences, 2016 Prize materials on contract theory.
* Michael C. Jensen & William H. Meckling, “Theory of the Firm” (1976), for agency-cost framing.
